// Title: Add Port Monitor Persistence in Registry
// ID: 944e8941-f6f6-4ee8-ac05-1c224e923c0e
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2021-12-30
// Tags: attack.privilege-escalation, attack.persistence, attack.t1547.010
// Description: Adversaries may use port monitors to run an attacker supplied DLL during system boot for persistence or privilege escalation.
// A port monitor can be set through the AddMonitor API call to set a DLL to be loaded at startup.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((where(TargetObject ICONTAINS "\\Control\\Print\\Monitors\\") AND where(Details IENDSWITH ".dll")) AND NOT (((where(Image = "C:\\Windows\\System32\\spoolsv.exe") AND where(TargetObject ICONTAINS "\\Control\\Print\\Monitors\\CutePDF Writer Monitor v4.0\\Driver") AND where(Details = "cpwmon64_v40.dll") AND (where(User ICONTAINS "AUTHORI") OR where(User ICONTAINS "AUTORI"))) OR (where(TargetObject ICONTAINS "\\Control\\Print\\Monitors\\MONVNC\\Driver")) OR ((where(TargetObject ICONTAINS "Control\\Print\\Environments\\") AND where(TargetObject ICONTAINS "\\Drivers\\") AND where(TargetObject ICONTAINS "\\VNC Printer"))))))
